{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20106",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.95,
      "end_seconds": 5.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "hello? Doctor? I was told to come in"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.02,
      "end_seconds": 10.79,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "okay, of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 11.42,
      "end_seconds": 24.7,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "uh thank you for fitting us in doctor it's some chest discomfort when I climb stairs doctor he didn't want to to come but I insisted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.14,
      "end_seconds": 28.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "Did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.37,
      "end_seconds": 32.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I I'd say three days maybe"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 33.12,
      "end_seconds": 36.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "hm, I'd say more like five days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.22,
      "end_seconds": 42.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.93,
      "end_seconds": 48.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "I suppose so, you know, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.5,
      "end_seconds": 59.75,
      "duration_seconds": 9.25,
      "text": "can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.74,
      "end_seconds": 68.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "Maybe a seven out of ten on a bad day. Yes stairs. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.97,
      "end_seconds": 72.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.97,
      "end_seconds": 88.2,
      "duration_seconds": 15.23,
      "text": "it, It usually comes with bruising easily sorry, what was I saying, as for bruising easily, I honestly can't say when that began it might have been last month or the month before"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.84,
      "end_seconds": 90.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Have you had nose bleeds?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 94.98,
      "end_seconds": 99.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.89,
      "text": "Oh, yes, about the same, nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.24,
      "end_seconds": 105.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Yes, carry on. Any pain at rest or fainting at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.69,
      "end_seconds": 108.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 110.73,
      "end_seconds": 115.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "have you noticed blood in the urine, black stools or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.83,
      "end_seconds": 123.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "sorry, uh, what was I saying, no, not a single one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.78,
      "end_seconds": 128.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.05,
      "end_seconds": 131.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Nothing else aches."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.92,
      "end_seconds": 137.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "So, is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.26,
      "end_seconds": 140.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "my father has Parkinson's disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.7,
      "end_seconds": 148.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.27,
      "end_seconds": 153.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "no, not that I know of"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.29,
      "end_seconds": 155.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.24,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.32,
      "end_seconds": 159.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.1,
      "end_seconds": 164.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.14,
      "end_seconds": 171.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.27,
      "end_seconds": 174.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.31,
      "end_seconds": 184.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.29,
      "end_seconds": 192.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.22,
      "end_seconds": 207.25,
      "duration_seconds": 14.03,
      "text": "I have diabetes i have heart disease, for two years i have high cholesterol, for nearly five years i did try to ignore it for a while"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.97,
      "end_seconds": 217.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Okay, I can see heart disease in your file as well. What do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.47,
      "end_seconds": 231.56,
      "duration_seconds": 10.09,
      "text": "I take sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day for my sugar. I'm on metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.38,
      "end_seconds": 250.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "can I check a few measurements before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.09,
      "end_seconds": 263.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "okay this won't take long.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.2,
      "end_seconds": 285.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.16,
      "text": "okay: pulse 85, temperature is 36.8 degrees, saturation 97 percent, BP is 113 over 78."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.44,
      "end_seconds": 289.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.71,
      "end_seconds": 293.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.91,
      "end_seconds": 300.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "I'd like to check you over now, if that's alright"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.9,
      "end_seconds": 303.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.22,
      "text": "does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.77,
      "end_seconds": 323.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.03,
      "end_seconds": 326.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "breathe out slowly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.3,
      "end_seconds": 340.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "there are a a few small bruises on your forearms"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.46,
      "end_seconds": 346.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.81,
      "end_seconds": 392.14,
      "duration_seconds": 29.33,
      "text": "Having listened and examined, I think we're dealing with stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding at this stage. I can't rule out reflux from the tablets yet. Let's get an ECG, for chest discomfort. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for bruising and bleeding. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 393.78,
      "end_seconds": 402.24,
      "duration_seconds": 8.46,
      "text": "I'm going to put you on pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. That's for stomach protection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.13,
      "end_seconds": 406.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.44,
      "end_seconds": 418.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.81,
      "text": "take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own. I'll want another look in six weeks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.66,
      "end_seconds": 422.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Yes you know that's manageable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 423.99,
      "end_seconds": 428.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.3,
      "end_seconds": 432.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "well, I think I understand everything thanks"
    }
  ]
}